Z||000001||loafer87gt||06-25-2001||11:09 PM||||It depends on what kind. The old 4 banger Fieros would get hammered pretty bad by any 1.8 Integra, but a GT should be able to take any RS and GS. A GSR has more HP than a GT, but our tourqey V6 should be able to give them a good run for their money. I wouldn't bother with the Type-R's, as they are low seven 7 second 0-60 cars and are pretty quick.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||06-25-2001||11:21 PM||||Type R's are mid 6 sec to 60 cars , 195Hp , 130??ft lbns (or there abouts) ft lbs of torque. They have a slight weight advantage.<P>The Type R's run low low 15's , high high 14's stock<P>Faster than a Stock GT....<BR>I have run up against a friends GSR and beat him , but his car is quick.<BR>JM<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">      <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals. &lt;b&gt; New White Face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS&lt;/b&gt;Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000003||filthyscarecrow||06-25-2001||11:59 PM||||i have one of each. a 94 integra RS (with some mods- only the ones that count) and an 86 SE (same v-6, slightly lighter than the GT) <P>are you ready? are you really ready? the integra still wins. the fiero is fast off the line, but it's power band is worthless compared to the integra. those of you who think that low end power is better for racing... think again. the integra pulls pretty well at low end too- especially the RS because it makes more torque sooner than the GS-R and type R. launches are really fast- almost as good as the fiero. and when it hits 3500rpm, kiss it g'bye. it f***ing SCREAMS up to 7000 rpm, pulling harder and harder all the way. the fiero has a slight cornering advantage (they feel pretty similar right now, and i have a set of bigger bars about to go on the acura. this area of my fiero has already been upgraded...) but what really makes the integra faster is that the gearbox drops the engine right at the start of the powerband each time i shift. and i can shift it faster than i can the fiero. fieros were great cars, but i think they're past their prime. at least stock ones... i'd take a 3800SC or turbo Quad4 over the teg anyday : ) <BR>  the teg is also more mild mannered. it's easier to drive civilised when necessary. they weigh about the same (roughly 2700 lbs) and the RS makes has 140-150 hp stock (mine's got like 160-165, adn i'm thinkin turbo in the near future...) the teg rolls more than the figaro in the corners, but the limit of adhesion is about the same. turn-in  feels much better in the figaro, but i think that might change with the bigger bars in the teg. my integra can EASILY whoop any fiero's arse under braking. unless you have some whopping wilwoods, don't even try to outbrake me. <BR>  the stock pedal layout is similar to the figaro too. they are a little too far apart for good heel-toe downshifting, but i made some pedal pads out of scrap aluminum that should take care of that. the teg revs faster than the figaro too. the revs come up about the same, but the throttle response is way better (even though the teg shuts off the fuel injection when the throttle plate closes anywhere above idle- this is why i get 35mpg even reving to 7k). <BR>  i also think the teg sounds cooler. i don't know where people get the "buzzing" stereotype... mine sounds a lot like the mid 80's F1 cars when it gets up around 5k, and under hard driving, that's where it stays. i've said it before, and i'll say it again: HONDA ENGINEERS KICKASS ENGINES. i would love to drop one in the back of the figaro. they're all aluminum block and cylinder heads, and would weigh less than anything else you could put in except maybe a weed eater engine, but would have better potential. i know people will argue with me, and disagree, but lemme ask you this: how much time do you have behind the wheels of both? i think i'm a bit of an expert on this one...<BR>the only thing i don't like is the inside wheel spinning coming out of corners. but the GS-R nad type R have limited slip diffs, so they won't do it. <BR>  the fiero has a much better driving position i.e. lying down, and i've never been able to get the seat quite right in the teg. the steering wheel's too big too, but as soon as i find a hub, the momo's comign off the figaro and onto the teg. i actually like the power steering on the integra too. it's not intrusive and deadening like most cars. i can still feel the bumps and channels in the road. <BR>i think the best part about the integra is that it can be abused. fieros can't. ask my friend ryan, who beat his and blew it up twice in one summer. i've hit the rev limiter i don't know how many times in the acura and it still runs like new. no weird noises. still smooth as silk. <P>here's what i'm sure everyone will hate me for: i'm thinking of sellin the fiero. it would break my heart to do it, because it was originally my dad's. i inherited it when he killed himself last year (they were one of our many common interests, and he loved it more than my mom unfortunately...), but i need the money. any ideas on ways to get around selling it?<P>hmm, this was really long... <P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...||||reg||1
