Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||06-26-2001||12:20 AM||||??? an RS????<BR> <P>I have run solo 1's Since  the New style integra came out with a mild modded 86 GT and walked all over RS's and a lot of GSR's. Type R's don;t even pull away that much. Anyone who has seen me run track events or divisionals knows that my car and a few other fiero racers like Doug chase , George Ryan and bert sager all drive the hell out of our cars. There built like tanks and the old 2.8 is good for low end grunt, even after high miles.<P><BR>I will have to get a hold of some video hardware to convert the Solo 1 and track events into avi format.<P>if you look at the #'s the RS pulls 8's to 60 , no offense , I got to drive some of the first new style Integra's on the shore. They handle excellently , but I wouldn't put a RS against a GT , unless the GT wasn't running right (manual car). I have had a lot of experience racing (autocrosses and track events) <P>the industry book I have here says the RS is a mid 16 sec car in the 1/4 , putting it inline with an automatic v6 Fiero...<P>Granted the brakes are better on an integra , but it wouldnd'nt take willwoods to put it in line with an integra. my 11.25" setup runs 4 piston willwoods up front , and from what I hear braking is on par with a new 911.<P>Just look at Stock Fiero racers like George Balzer. 15.2's out of a Bone stock 2.8 ..Type R's run right around 15 flat<P>Hope no offense is taken<P>HP sells cars<BR>Torque wins races...<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">      <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals. &lt;b&gt; New White Face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS&lt;/b&gt;Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
