Z||000011||filthyscarecrow||06-27-2001||01:57 AM||||no offense taken. but please understand, i do know a thing or two about making a car go fast. i helped design and build the U of M formuloa SAE car and i've had plenty of racing experience. my guess is that the RS's and GSRs you've been walking all over just plain dno't know how to drive. you must be an excellent driver as well to make a fiero go that fast without losing it. keep in mind too that my RS isn't exactly stock. i've got some intake and exhaust mods that are worth quite a bit of high end hp. it wasn't that great when i first bought it either, but they're really easy to work on, and go-fast parts (not ricer parts) are cheap and readily available. when i get the turbo system designed and on the car, it'll waste a type R as well. it's all a matter of perspective. they are both great cars to drive, but if i had to race one, i would take the integra for all the reasons stated in my earlier post- especially the reliability and gas milage ones. i love all types of cars. and to fierodude, hating any type of car becasue of where it comes from displays the same ignorance as blatant racism. if you can't tell me WHY it's jap crap, then maybe you need to silence thy piehole until you have something intelligent and worthwhile to say. but that's just my opinion...<BR>and my teg will take your GT anyday : ) <P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...||||reg||1
Z||000012||TRiAD||06-27-2001||06:24 AM||||Motor Trend's 3-88 article on the '88 GT rates the fastest Fiero (stock), the -88 GT 5sp at <B>0-60 in 8.72sec</B> (pretty sad, really). <P>A late-model Acura Integra GS-R will run <B>0-60 in 7.2sec</B> (stock). (R&T 11-99)<P>A .5sec difference to 60 is considered <I>substantial</I> by most automotive journalists, and it's a hard 1.5sec to make up. <P>Fact is, any Civic with the D16Z6 (1.6l SOHC VTEC; the EX, 5th gen Si...) will run 0-60 in 8.0sec, and the DOHC 1.6 (B16; late Si, del Sol VTEC) will be between the other Civics and the GS-R. <P>The Fiero can be made to be fast, but we're working with a LOT less "raw material than the Honda guys...<P>Your Mission, should you choose to accept it...<P><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||6
