Z||000014||Slammed Fiero||06-27-2001||09:31 AM||||The One GSR I have the video of was driven by Marc White , whom is a national champ , I think he knows how to drive after 12 national championships in solo 1 and 2.<P>As for 0 to 60 , read my sig , thats all that is done to my motor. I pulled a couple 6.5 sec 0 to 60 runs fiero Fierolisa as a witness riding shotgun (GTEC). Your intake and exhaust no doubt create power. But by the time you get into your power band , the low end grunt of a well tuned 2.8 has left you at the lights. (I have a 4spd , not a getrag)<P>Magazines don;t really mean much IMHO ..they provide a baseline. <P>As for jap car bashing ,I totally agree , there marvels of technology. I had an 88 Civic and I loved it until the poor thing rotted out (it was a beater) but it still ran perfectly afer 160,000 miles, 15,000 of those miles were on a blown head gasket.<P>JM<P><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">       <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
