Z||000017||Slammed Fiero||06-27-2001||06:34 PM||||255/40/17 Pirelli P zero's for a hard launch<BR>New-ish clutch.<BR>No cat converter<BR>short shifter<P>No idea really either. I thought it was a fluke first time. But I did it several Times when I used chris Moores Gtec , with Lisa in the car , and with her not int he car. (Hot hot hot day) at Norwalk ohio<P><BR>Then I thought to myself ..perhaps it;s the GTEC. So I borrowed my local autocross clubs GTEC.<P>11 at night late august , fairly cool , mid to high 6's again. Best being 6.54. The problem this night was traction ,  it spun in 1st with any sort of launch.<P>the best i have heard is a friend (Steve Huskins) Turning 6.4 to 60 , with a 4spd 85 GT , he has ocelot exhaust , MSD ignition , I forget what else. The car has 16" wheels , koni's , no cat converter, very good driver.<P>So if it happened once I would say fluke , baseline for me is around 6.7-6.8 seconds. Abusive launch I can get the 6.5's. I have a new set of Kuhomo Victoracer autocross tires on the way. I can launch even harder.<P>When I get the NOS installed I will go out and GTEC the car again. My only disadvantage this time will be bigger brakes , which = weight.<P><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">       <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
