Z||000019||88formula||06-27-2001||07:29 PM||||Best I could get with Dyno2000 and Drapstrip2000 was 0-60 in 6.8 seconds with 160 horsepower. I used a super high 4000-rpm launch with the most perfect track conditions. <P>But hey what I have is a computer program and what you have is the real thing. I would say you have a killer 2.8. I bet you have light wheels too. I wish you lived near me!   <P>Thanks Slam. <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Slammed Fiero||06-27-2001||07:49 PM||||No idea , my 17's are Factory height. The wheels are 17's the tires are low profile so they compensate for the height.<P>The car has 40,000 miles on it and is well taken care of. Runs no cat converter , Redline synthetic oil. The wheels weigh within 2lbs each of the factory ones (yes I weighted)  The suspension helps to launch the car well.<P>It may seem off , but 2 different Gtecs , 2 Different countries don't lie.<P>I have turned mid 6's on several different passes and have been using GTECS for around 4 years now , First time was at the 1997 michigan fiero fest , I used steve huskins. got low 7's there, with a mostly stock car.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">       <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
